 JSON in, JSON out. Routes are listed in `README.md`.

+## Authentication and roles
+
+Requests carry `Authorization: Bearer <key>`, matched against `apiKeys` in the
+store (`{ key, name, role }`).
+
+- `viewer`: may only read (`GET`, except `GET /audit`).
+- `cook`: may read, and may also cook recipes (`POST /recipes/:id/cook`),
+  record waste (`POST /batches/:id/waste`), log temperatures
+  (`POST /temperatures`) and enter stock-take counts
+  (`POST /stocktakes/:id/counts`).
+- `manager`: may call every route, including `GET /audit`.
+
+A missing or unknown key returns `401` (`unauthorized`); a known key without
+permission returns `403` (`forbidden`). Every request that changes data writes
+an audit entry listed newest first by `GET /audit` (managers only).
+
 ## Errors

 Errors have a status from `src/errors.js` and the body
